WEBVTT

00:00.280 --> 00:01.800
Hello everyone.

00:01.800 --> 00:04.120
Many companies are deploying AI to

00:04.120 --> 00:06.600
solve yesterday's problems. In this

00:06.600 --> 00:07.960
short series, I want to talk

00:07.960 --> 00:09.719
about vision.

00:09.719 --> 00:11.360
Four design principles to build a

00:11.360 --> 00:13.440
future of work that is not only

00:13.440 --> 00:16.000
actionable, but truly desirable.

00:16.860 --> 00:18.301
Our future is being shaped by

00:18.301 --> 00:21.221
systemic mega trends, four major

00:21.221 --> 00:23.340
forces that every company needs to

00:23.340 --> 00:24.421
be ready for.

00:25.121 --> 00:27.002
First, a unique generational

00:27.002 --> 00:29.362
crossover as digital natives enter

00:29.362 --> 00:30.442
the workforce.

00:31.183 --> 00:33.543
Second, a post-COVID shift in our

00:33.543 --> 00:35.503
relationship to work. It concerns

00:35.503 --> 00:36.983
all of us, but especially the new

00:36.983 --> 00:37.983
generations.

00:38.724 --> 00:40.684
Third, a complete reset of our

00:40.684 --> 00:43.684
digital ecosystem by AI. A true

00:43.684 --> 00:45.763
industrial revolution, bringing both

00:45.763 --> 00:47.804
hopes and fears for the workforce.

00:48.504 --> 00:50.225
And fourth, a world full of

00:50.225 --> 00:52.945
uncertainty, where change has never

00:52.945 --> 00:54.185
been so fast.

00:54.385 --> 00:56.706
Together, these megatrends create a

00:56.706 --> 00:59.186
dual challenge. On one side, a

00:59.186 --> 01:00.746
productivity and operating

01:00.746 --> 01:03.146
challenge. On the other, a human

01:03.146 --> 01:05.266
and cultural one.

01:05.266 --> 01:07.066
Our operating models were built

01:07.066 --> 01:08.666
for a stability that no longer

01:08.666 --> 01:12.026
exists. Today, business agility is

01:12.026 --> 01:13.306
the new baseline.

01:13.307 --> 01:15.266
Put together, the picture becomes

01:15.266 --> 01:17.747
clear. Fragmented solutions will

01:17.747 --> 01:19.066
not solve these underlying

01:19.066 --> 01:21.667
challenges. We need one unified

01:21.667 --> 01:23.707
operating system, able to address

01:23.707 --> 01:24.867
them all at once.

01:25.108 --> 01:27.588
This is the AI paradox. More

01:27.588 --> 01:29.948
human, more digital. It is not a

01:29.948 --> 01:32.627
trade-off. It is AND. We use the

01:32.627 --> 01:34.868
power of AI to free up space so

01:34.868 --> 01:37.268
that we can be more human.

01:37.549 --> 01:39.709
That is why I propose four

01:39.709 --> 01:42.309
shifts, four design principles,

01:42.309 --> 01:44.068
from talented individuals to

01:44.068 --> 01:46.509
talented teams, from transactions

01:46.509 --> 01:48.389
to moments that matter,

01:48.389 --> 01:50.429
from tech magic to LeanAI

01:50.429 --> 01:51.988
transformation

01:51.988 --> 01:53.909
and from resource management to a

01:53.909 --> 01:56.229
workforce digital twin.

01:56.229 --> 01:58.549
One episode for each shift.

01:58.790 --> 02:01.229
Next episode, why talent is no

02:01.229 --> 02:03.150
longer an individual story but a

02:03.150 --> 02:04.310
team sport.
